--TEST--
A constructor's `return` carries no value, while a bare `return;` still leaves it early (`rule:php-migration/a-constructor-return-carries-no-value`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:php-migration/a-constructor-return-carries-no-value`: the object under
// construction is the result, so a value here has nowhere to go. The early
// exit is untouched — the bare `return;` above the refused line is not
// reported, and `rule:classes/definite-property-initialization` goes on
// checking that path.
class Point {
    public int $x;

    public function constructor(int $x) {
        $this->x = $x;
        if ($x == 0) {
            return;
        }
        return $x;
    }
}

var $p = new Point(1);
echo $p->x, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0248]: a constructor's `return` carries no value
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
